{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["Your animal you shall not mate as mixed kinds — according to the way of the world and as a response to the heretics: just as Scripture commanded that each and every thing produce fruit after its kind, as in the works of Creation, so it commanded to conduct the world accordingly with animals in the fields and with trees, and also in plowing with an ox and a donkey, which are two species. And also with wool and linen, since this is a species of animals and that is a species of ground and its produce. And by 'kinds' I say: the wool is dyed and the linen is not dyed, and He is strict about a garment of two appearances, and they conceded to me."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The lemma cited is from the latter part of the verse (כלאים); Rashbam's comment addresses the entire verse. The phrase ותשובת המינין is rendered as 'a response to the heretics'; the reference and scope of the second-person 'they conceded to me' (והודו לי) is unspecified in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:06.343219681Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}